  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14178864/assets/d46182f3d4373a6b8bb1d330afb51a4ed2eea0c33b2f929b5538d7e0edf76353.png)\n\nGiven that $ABCDE≅MPQRT,$ find $x-2y.$",
  "worked_solution": "The statement $ABCDE≅MPQRT$ means that $P$ and $Q$ are congruent. Moreover,\n\n- vertex $A$ corresponds to vertex $M,$\n\n- vertex $B$ corresponds to vertex $P,$\n\n- vertex $C$ corresponds to vertex $Q,$\n\n- vertex $D$ corresponds to vertex $R,$\n\n- vertex $E$ corresponds to vertex $T.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}MP & =AB \\\\ y-4 & =2 \\\\ y & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠E & =m∠T \\\\ {(3x+20)}^{∘} & ={140}^{∘} \\\\ 3x+20 & =140 \\\\ 3x & =120 \\\\ x & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nx-2y=40-12=28.\n$$",
